      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "Step 3.1 says the restricted resolution is “by objects which are injective,” citing only that restriction is exact. Exactness alone does not imply that injectives remain injective. The short missing justification is available from `thm-extension-by-zero-adjunction-exactness`: for an open inclusion, extension by zero is exact and left adjoint to restriction, so restriction preserves injectives. This is an immediately closable proof gap.",
